WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:26.400
Let's talk today about the concept of the
lesser of two evils.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:33.980
Are you evil if you choose the lesser of two
evils, or should you abstain altogether from

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:35.650
being involved in such a choice?

00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:40.360
Now, of course, the context of all of this
is that there are people saying they're not

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:45.780
going to vote for Joe Biden instead of Donald
Trump, because Joe Biden is merely the lesser

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:47.030
of two evils.

00:00:47.030 --> 00:00:52.550
There are people who see both Biden and Trump
as evils, although maybe to different degrees,

00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:55.920
and voting for any evil would not be OK for
them.

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:59.710
So they might abstain or they might vote third
party or write someone in or whatever the

00:00:59.710 --> 00:01:01.500
case may be.

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:07.040
Another way that some are saying it is those
who are focusing in on the sexual assault

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:09.730
component of the current political race.

00:01:09.730 --> 00:01:12.840
There are people who write to me and say,
David, are you just saying I should choose

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:18.460
which sexual assault or I want either vote
for a sexual assault or with one allegation

00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:21.720
against them or a sexual assault or with 26?

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:23.780
That's not a good choice for me.

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:25.920
I'm going to opt out.

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:29.380
So let's really think this through and take
it in pieces.

00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:36.310
There's this first question of just arguing
like, is Biden evil or is Biden not that good?

00:01:36.310 --> 00:01:40.720
Or like what what what exactly is the characterization
of Biden in this context?

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:43.240
I'm going to argue that it doesn't matter
to me.

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:49.039
It's a distraction to say, is Biden good or
simply less evil than Donald Trump?

00:01:49.039 --> 00:01:55.179
Once you grant that Biden is better than Trump,
if you don't then vote for Trump, then there's

00:01:55.179 --> 00:01:56.410
not even a conversation.

00:01:56.410 --> 00:01:59.260
If you think Trump's better vote, vote for
Trump, that's clear.

00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:04.819
But once you grant Biden is better than Trump,
I don't think it matters whether Biden is

00:02:04.819 --> 00:02:08.739
less evil or good for the purposes of the
conversation we're going to have today.

00:02:08.739 --> 00:02:11.880
Secondly, and this is really important.

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:15.490
The concept of opting out because you can't
vote for evil.

00:02:15.490 --> 00:02:17.270
There is no opting out here, folks.

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:22.500
If you're an American and you are allowed
to vote, there is no opting out.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:25.470
You can choose not to cast a ballot.

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:31.069
But from a left of Trump perspective, either
way you're participating, you're influencing.

00:02:31.069 --> 00:02:37.240
You have a say, a stake, and you are you are
affecting the outcome, whether you cast the

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:38.400
ballot or not.

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:44.530
There are people making themselves sort of
feel okay about not voting for Biden by simply

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:46.040
saying I'm opting out.

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:50.810
I don't like the choices, so I'm not going
to participate in a literal sense.

00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:57.459
You aren't taking the act of voting and going
and doing it, but you're not opting out of

00:02:57.459 --> 00:02:58.650
the process.

00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:03.030
If you vote for Trump, that's obviously a
vote against Biden.

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:09.209
If you don't vote at all and believe Biden
is less bad than Trump, but not good enough

00:03:09.209 --> 00:03:12.040
for you to vote for him, you're still helping
Trump with one vote.

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:16.140
It's a vote that Trump does not need to overcome
in order to be reelected.

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:19.030
So let's really cut through the B.S. here.

00:03:19.030 --> 00:03:21.920
Biden being evil or not isn't relevant.

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:27.269
If we agree he's better than Trump for our
purposes today, that's all that matters.

00:03:27.269 --> 00:03:32.200
Opting out and being a non-actor in the process
is a rejection of both candidates.

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:37.080
Unless you renounce your citizenship and aren't
allowed to vote, you have a vote.

00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:41.340
Whether you use it or not, you are participating
and your actions are part of the ultimate

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:42.340
consequence.

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:46.540
So given all of that, this is actually quite
simple.

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:51.909
If you were put in a room with two buttons,
one button kills 10 people and one button

00:03:51.909 --> 00:03:54.040
kills a million people.

00:03:54.040 --> 00:04:00.040
And if you say I'm not going to press a button,
someone else can press the button for me.

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:04.989
Is there any question that you are acting
in a way that is improper?

00:04:04.989 --> 00:04:09.469
Is there any question that you should obviously
press the button, given that one of these

00:04:09.469 --> 00:04:11.510
two buttons is going to be pressed?

00:04:11.510 --> 00:04:17.070
That saves nine hundred and ninety nine thousand
nine hundred and ninety people.

00:04:17.070 --> 00:04:18.070
Right.

00:04:18.070 --> 00:04:20.579
Nine nine nine nine nine zero people.

00:04:20.579 --> 00:04:22.560
Of course, you should press that button.

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:25.680
That would be choosing between the lesser
of two evils.

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:27.450
Killing 10 people is bad.

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:29.770
Killing one million people is also bad.

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:34.730
And I would argue it is worse, but it actually,
again, doesn't matter whether you're choosing

00:04:34.730 --> 00:04:36.600
between two evils.

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:40.120
Because think about a slightly different scenario
than the one I just gave you.

00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:41.580
You're in the same room.

00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:43.169
There are also two buttons.

00:04:43.169 --> 00:04:49.479
One button kills a million people and the
other kills no one and resurrects one person.

00:04:49.479 --> 00:04:52.139
It brings back someone that died of a car
accident.

00:04:52.139 --> 00:04:53.139
OK.

00:04:53.139 --> 00:04:56.140
Imagine that isn't the right action.

00:04:56.140 --> 00:04:58.380
Obvious in both cases.

00:04:58.380 --> 00:05:01.340
Resurrect one person versus kill 10 million.

00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:03.419
Kill 10 versus kill 10 million.

00:05:03.419 --> 00:05:04.419
Whatever the numbers are.

00:05:04.419 --> 00:05:05.419
Right.

00:05:05.419 --> 00:05:08.020
In either case, these are the choices.

00:05:08.020 --> 00:05:14.340
And if you say leave it up to chance, leave
it up to other people or I can take the action

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:16.910
that I know is the preferable action.

00:05:16.910 --> 00:05:19.759
Of course I take the preferable action anytime
now.

00:05:19.759 --> 00:05:25.580
How do you justify taking any action that
could let other people press the kill a million

00:05:25.580 --> 00:05:26.580
button?

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:29.350
In either case, I don't know how you justify
that.

00:05:29.350 --> 00:05:35.259
This is why the debate about is Biden sort
of good but not that good versus is Biden

00:05:35.259 --> 00:05:37.190
less bad than Trump?

00:05:37.190 --> 00:05:38.490
It's irrelevant.

00:05:38.490 --> 00:05:44.080
There is no responsible way to say I'm going
to let other people choose and I won't put

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:47.740
in my vote for the less bad or better option.

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:53.780
But if that was the full analysis, I would
be doing a disservice to this discussion.

00:05:53.780 --> 00:05:59.039
There are philosophical structures that would
defend not pressing any button.

00:05:59.039 --> 00:06:02.780
So I've sort of given you a more utilitarian
perspective.

00:06:02.780 --> 00:06:05.479
But let's consider for a second.

00:06:05.479 --> 00:06:12.220
The philosophy of Immanuel Kant, Kantian ism,
German philosopher from mostly the 18th century,

00:06:12.220 --> 00:06:15.639
died in the first few years of the 19th century,
I believe.

00:06:15.639 --> 00:06:20.009
You could certainly take a look at Kantian
ism, which is focused not on end goals like

00:06:20.009 --> 00:06:24.330
I'm looking at the end goal when I say if
10 or a million are going to die, let me do

00:06:24.330 --> 00:06:30.430
what I can to make it 10 instead of a million
Kantian ism instead of focusing on the end

00:06:30.430 --> 00:06:37.539
goal would deal more with one's duty and acting
in accordance with underlying principles.

00:06:37.539 --> 00:06:44.610
So if we focus on this lesser of two evils
idea and we look at it in terms of the principle,

00:06:44.610 --> 00:06:50.680
one could have a Kantian aligned principle
of I'm not going to vote for bad people, that

00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:56.830
I'm only going to exercise my vote when I
have someone good to vote for because of a

00:06:56.830 --> 00:07:02.280
principle, I'm not going to do the utilitarian
focus on the end goal of killing fewer people.

00:07:02.280 --> 00:07:08.530
I'm going to justify not pressing either button
because it would violate a principle of mine

00:07:08.530 --> 00:07:12.930
rather than focusing on the harm reduction
utilitarian component.

00:07:12.930 --> 00:07:16.620
But that's a fair argument that that would
be right out of Kantian ism.

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:23.930
I believe that even in this case, even in
this strict Kantian defense of the nonvotes

00:07:23.930 --> 00:07:29.110
to adhere to a principle, I think it still
falls apart because in the case of voting

00:07:29.110 --> 00:07:35.229
or not voting in the United States, both actions
are a form of participation.

00:07:35.229 --> 00:07:39.030
Once again, whether you vote or not, you're
participating either way.

00:07:39.030 --> 00:07:44.390
And what I mean by that is that the act of
voting in and of itself, like the cat, filling

00:07:44.390 --> 00:07:49.030
out your ballot, mailing it in whatever it
is, in a moral sense, neutral.

00:07:49.030 --> 00:07:50.030
Right.

00:07:50.030 --> 00:07:51.229
Just filling out a piece of paper.

00:07:51.229 --> 00:07:54.759
You're either filling out the piece of paper
or you're not filling out the piece of paper.

00:07:54.759 --> 00:07:59.520
But once you understand that, either way,
you're participating in deciding the outcome.

00:07:59.520 --> 00:08:02.550
You're no less of a participant by not voting.

00:08:02.550 --> 00:08:07.750
You are no more adhering to the principle
that you were trying to adhere to in this

00:08:07.750 --> 00:08:13.370
county in sense by not voting, whether you
vote for Trump or merely don't get in the

00:08:13.370 --> 00:08:19.110
way of Trump by not voting, you are still
participating because voting is a right that

00:08:19.110 --> 00:08:20.620
you have as an American.

00:08:20.620 --> 00:08:26.180
You are either way participating in the outcome
and thus the non vote might make people feel

00:08:26.180 --> 00:08:32.219
like they're opting out over principles and
having no impact, choosing not to participate.

00:08:32.219 --> 00:08:36.729
But in reality, you are just as much of a
participant, whether you vote or not.

00:08:36.729 --> 00:08:43.390
And thus even a Kantian ethic of adhering
to principles rather than focusing on utilitarian

00:08:43.390 --> 00:08:47.140
end goals fails to justify a non vote.

00:08:47.140 --> 00:08:49.432
In this case, let me know where I'm going
wrong.

00:08:49.432 --> 00:08:49.450
I look forward to the discussion.

